## Appendix — Language Specification (folded from `SPEC.oot` 2026-08-12)

> `SPEC.oot` is folded here. `DESIGN.oot` is the single north star + spec. See git history for `SPEC.oot`.
> This file is 311 lines before appendix — combined >256, exceeds RULES §1.7. Keep as exception for north star, or split appendix to `DESIGN_SPEC_APPENDIX.oot` later.

### A1. Core Vision & Design Philosophy (from SPEC)

- File extension is `.oo` (`main.oo`, `auth.oo`).
- Rapid loop `check` / `build` / `run` is real on alpha. Sub-second marketing is not proven. **[STATUS: residual — see `OODA_SPEED.md`]**
- Safety without friction — bad code fails to compile, but without extra ceremony.
- Self-testing code — contracts and tests live with the function.
- AI vibe-coding native — machine-readable AST diagnostics, strict contracts, instant feedback.
- Zero-dependency ecosystem — compiler + CLI ship together. Package, LSP, and registry are not yet a single toolchain. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A2. Type System & Expressiveness

- Variables are immutable `let` unless `let mut`.
- No `null`. Use `Option[T]` and `Result[T, E]` with exhaustive `match`.
- Strong static typing with local inference.
- Traits over inheritance.
- Refinement types — Goal: `type Port = Int where 1..=65535`. Not yet compile-time. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Strong newtypes — Goal: `type UserId = newtype u64` to avoid mixing IDs. Not yet full surface. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A3. Guard Rails & Security (from SPEC)

- Capability seals (Fs/Sys/Env/Net/Time/Rand/Alloc + ThreadCap/GpuCap) are in. Full biometric ladder is not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Must-use — unused `Result`/`Option`/resource is a hard error. Coverage is partial. **[STATUS: residual]**
- No null/wild pointers — RAII and ARC aim to remove leaks, not yet proven full elimination. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A4. Self-Testing & Executable Contracts

- `requires` / `ensures` — simple runtime is in; synthesis not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**
- `@example` doc-tests — Goal: examples become tests. **[STATUS: residual]**
- `verify` blocks — pure `verify` path is in. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Fuzzing `#[auto_fuzz]` — pure int/bool/string/list domains are in. Attribute and full suite are not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A5. Memory & Concurrency Model

- RAII + region arenas — ARC on ref0 is in. Full region arena and 0ms marketing are later. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Structured concurrency — Goal: tasks bound to parent scopes. Channels/actors refused; ThreadCap partial. **[STATUS: residual / path-A refuse]**
- Zero data races — Not yet proven for full product. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A6. AI & Tooling Integration

- Machine-readable diagnostics `--json-errors` with `E_CAP` hints are in. Multi-code auto-fix is not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**
- `comptime` execution — Goal: build-time type gen with normal code. Names `macro_expand` / `ast_macro` refused. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A7. Unified Developer Toolchain

- `ooda build` / `run` / `check` — in, Backend-C floor.
- `ooda test` — pure verify and fuzz are in.
- `ooda fmt` / `lint` / `lsp` / `pkg` — goals, not full products on alpha. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A8. Syntax & Grammar Design

- Brace syntax `{}` with expression bodies (TypeScript readability + Rust safety).
- `if`, `match`, and blocks return values directly.
- Keywords `requires`, `ensures`, `spec` sit on or in the function header.

### A9. Compilation Target Architecture

- Floor: Backend-C (`emit-c` + `chs_rt` + gcc).
- LLVM IR — smoke only, not default. **[STATUS: residual]**
- WASM — smoke only, not production browser floor. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Instant JIT (`ooda run`) — Not a JIT. Native/BC run is real. Sub-second marketing is residual. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A10. Multi-Ecosystem Interoperability (FFI & Bridges)

- C-ABI FFI — Cap-gated `dlopen` stub is in; unrestricted zero-cost FFI and Rust LTO are not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Python bridge `embed "python"` — Stub only; `load_model` not working. **[STATUS: residual / fail-closed stub]**
- C-header auto-import `import_c` — Refused; no header reading. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A11. Zero-Shot AI Adaptability

- Compact grammar `ooda.grammar` — under 2,000 tokens goal; living `ooda.ebnf` exists. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Grammar-constrained decoding `ooda.gbnf` — file exists; sampler integration not yet.
- High orthogonality — one way to express each idea.
- Compiler-as-teacher — JSON error explains rule with example.
- Self-describing API `ooda reflect` — parse-only alpha. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A12. Architectural Constraints for LLM Context Optimization

- Zero-boilerplate FS modules — any `.oo` file is a module (`src/auth/jwt.oo` → `auth::jwt`).
- Modular-size lints — Warn at ~256–300 lines. Soft. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Isolated functional units — one file holds types + logic + caps + `verify`.
- Symbol reflection — Goal: `ooda context path#symbol`. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Module outlines `ooda outline` — parse-only alpha. **[STATUS: residual]**
- AST diff edits `ooda patch` — node-id patches residual. **[STATUS: aspirational]**
- Token-optimized diagnostics `--json-minimal` — residual. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A13. Comprehensive Security Architecture

- Capability sandboxing — default-deny seals are in. Full OS isolation and registry audit are not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Memory safety — RAII and ARC aim to remove UAF/overflow/null classes. Not yet proven full. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Injection prevention — `process::exec(sys_cap, "git", ["clone", user_input])` array form blocks shell injection.
- AI containment — caps trap I/O. JIT containment not a product (no JIT). **[STATUS: residual]**
- Zero-day defense — default-deny trapping is in; memory class defense and metamorphic layout (decoys only) are partial; supervisor trees later. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A14. High-Performance Engine Architecture

- 0ms GC — ARC is in; 0ms marketing residual. **[STATUS: residual]**
- LLVM optimizer & bare-metal — LLVM smoke only; bare-metal refused. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Monomorphized generics & value types — depth not full. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Zero-cost abstractions & strippable contracts — simple contracts are in; full strip in release residual. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Dual-engine execution — `run` native, `build` Backend-C. Marketing dual-engine residual. **[STATUS: residual]**

### A15. Telemetry, Logging & Debugging

- Structured logging & spans — Goal: `log::info!`. **[STATUS: residual]**
- AI-enriched stack traces — Full arg-value traces later. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Time-travel replay `ooda replay` — Goal; not shipped. **[STATUS: residual / not shipped]**
- Zero-overhead probes — Goal: `log::debug!` stripped in release unless enabled. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Performance profiler `ooda profile` — Goal; not shipped. **[STATUS: residual / not shipped]**

### A16. First Principles Foundation

- Code, contracts, and tests are one truth — one atomic unit.
- Cognition & LLM context are finite — grammar <2k tokens, files ~256 lines.
- Security is a capability, not sanitization — zero I/O by default.
- Memory lifetimes follow scopes — scope-based reclaim, O(1) free.
- Feedback speed drives quality — short `check/build/run` loops.

### A17. Governance, Ecosystem & Release Strategy

- Repo is public (`v0.184.0-alpha`); boards may be private. **Beta not claimed.** Ladder `v0.1.0-alpha → v0.5.0-beta → v0.9.0-rc → v1.0.0-stable` is aspirational.
- Std is growing (core vs os split; Result, MD5, net wrappers). Not yet HTTP-server-complete. **[STATUS: residual — crypto/math gated]**
- Lockfile governance `ooda.lock` — hashed lockfiles and capability-audited installs, not yet. **[STATUS: residual]**
- Process resilience & supervisor trees — Goal; refuse on alpha. **[STATUS: residual / path-A refuse]**
- Migration `ooda migrate` — Disabled (unsafe `let mut` sed removed). AST tool later. **[STATUS: disabled residual]**
- Standards / RPC / benchmarks — No shipping suite yet. **[STATUS: residual]**

---

## Glossary (plain words for jargon)

- **Path-A** — minimal safe stub that refuses the name on alpha. Not a full feature.
- **Residual** — intended but not yet true in the product. Listed honestly.
- **Refuse stub** — compiler says `ERR` if you use the name, so you cannot think it works.
- **Dual-green** — both host-built and product-built compilers pass the same smoke test.
- **Seal / Cap** — a permission token you must pass to a function to let it do I/O.
- **Alpha In** — works at least as a smoke test, not yet a full product.
- **ZT** — zero-trust checks from the audit phalanx.
